\DOC LOCAL_SUB_P521_TAC

\TYPE {LOCAL_SUB_P521_TAC : int -> string list -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Symbolically executes an inlined modular-subtraction subroutine call, advancing
the machine state in an {eventually} goal past that call and recording its
result as a new assumption.

\DESCRIBE
The first argument is an {int} selecting the code offset / instance of the call
site to discharge; the second is a {string list} naming the three operands of
the subtraction — the destination variable and the two source variables — from
which the new result assumption is built. The goal's conclusion is an
{eventually} property at a state {s_n}, with assumptions {A} describing {s_n}:
program counter value, {bytes_loaded}, register and memory-content reads, a
{MAYCHANGE} relation from the initial state, and accumulated arithmetic facts.
All state-specific assumptions about {s_n} (program counter, {bytes_loaded},
register and memory reads, and the {MAYCHANGE} frame) are replaced by the
corresponding assumptions about a fresh successor state {s_{n+1}}, with an
updated program-counter offset, a possibly enlarged {MAYCHANGE} frame covering
the written destination buffer, a new read assumption giving the destination
buffer the named result value, and a new conditional arithmetic assumption {t <
p /\ u < p ==> &d = (&t - &u) rem &p} for the three named operands.
{
   A, state facts about s_n ?- eventually ... s_n
   ================================================  LOCAL_SUB_P521_TAC n ["d"; "t"; "u"]
   A, state facts about s_{n+1},
      (t < p /\ u < p ==> &d = (&t - &u) rem &p)
   ?- eventually ... s_{n+1}
}

\COMMENTS
The observed traces show only this single-subgoal state-advancing behaviour,
always on goals of this {eventually} shape with a full set of state
assumptions.

\ENDDOC
